hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17996","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat one day in his palm and placed his finger upon it, then said, Allah said, Son of Adam, how do you defy Me, when I created you from the like of this. Until when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, with the earth groaning from you. Then you gathered and withheld, until when the soul reached the collarbones you said, I give charity, and when is the time of charity."
"17997","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat on his palm and said, Son of Adam, and he mentioned its meaning."
"17998","Abu al-Mughirah narrated it to us, Hariz narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat one day in his hand and placed his finger upon it, then said, Allah Almighty said, Son of Adam, how do you defy Me, when I created you from the like of this. Until when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, with the earth groaning from you. Then you gathered and withheld, until when the soul reached the collarbones you said, I give charity, and when is the time of charity."
"17999","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Maysarah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, and he mentioned it, and he did not say, Allah Almighty said, and he said, and when is the time of charity."
